een  infectious and non-infectious diseases  which as we know infectious disease is  spread through context that is from  person to person and it is contagious  and it is spreaded by pathogenic  microorganisms like virus bacteria  parasites fungi  non-infectious diseases are non-contact  use and deadline spread by  contact further they are spreaded by  environmental  factors nutritional deficiencies genetic  inheritance mutations lifestyles etc  there is a particular way by how  pathogens spread  it might be by replication in their own  breed or colonization in particular  environment it can be due to cell death  and there can be a chance of bacteria or  virus entering into our immune system  because certain types of immune cells  are dead  it can also be due to organ function  damage or the release of certain harmful  toxins which can prevent the  use of certain microbes into our body  this is the whole picture i have  picturized this is  used to understand first how the  pathogens  interact and replicate what techniques  are used for the sequencing  the genome sequence and the application  of the genome sequencing now we know  that  ngs is a system that transforms the  data sequences the genome sequences into  data file formats like fasta fast q  bam metron etc so further these genomes  of  of say of any pathogen is further used  for getting a pure insight into  virulence capacity of that particular  parasite  it is also used for studying the protein  expression and using this protein  expression vaccine design and drug  design is done  they're also used to study the  population structure and evolutionary  history of that particular parasite  which gives a comparative analysis of  genome sequencing  and strains of same species if they're  involved or not  are more violent or not it is also used  for studying specific sequences of  strain detection  it is also used for diagnostic purposes  of how they have used by  pcr address or dna microarrays and  proteins are i